<title>ECUADOR: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>ECUADOR GOVERNMENT LIST (970209)</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p>* 9 Feb 97 - President Bucaram finally conceded defeat in    *</p>
<p>* the presidential crisis, saying he had been		    *</p>
<p>* deposed in a &quot;congressional coup&quot; that was		     *</p>
<p>* backed by the country's armed forces.			    *</p>
<p>* Lawmakers and military leaders agreed on a plan		* </p>
<p>* allowing Vice President Arteaga to take over as		* </p>
<p>* interim president, but congressional leader		    * </p>
<p>* Fabian Alarcon, who was initially voted by		     * </p>
<p>* Congress to replace Bucaram, was expected to be		* </p>
<p>* re-appointed acting president within a matter of days.     *</p>
<p>**************************************************************</p>
<p>President (Interim) &amp; Vice President..........Rosalia ARTEAGA</p>
<p>							  (**SEE NOTE ABOVE)</p>
<p>- - - - - - - CABINET (10 Aug 96)</p>
<p> Agriculture.......Hugo ENCALADA</p>
<p> Defence (acting).............Gen. Paco MONCAYO</p>
<p> Education.......Sandra CORREA**</p>
<p>						   (** Resigned 28 Jan 97)</p>
<p> Energy...........Alfredo ADUM**</p>
<p>						    (** Resigned 6 Feb 97)</p>
<p> Environment...............Jaime Galarza ZAVALA</p>
<p> Finance............Pablo CONCHA</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs..............Galo Leoro FRANCO</p>
<p> Government Minister.............Frank VARGAS**</p>
<p>						    (** Resigned 6 Feb 97)</p>
<p> Housing &amp; Urban Development..............Victor Hugo SICOURET</p>
<p> Industry............Jorge MARUN</p>
<p> Labour.......Hugo LARREA Romero</p>
<p> Public Health......Marcelo CRUZ</p>
<p>Public Works....Vicente ESTRADA  Social Welfare................Adolfo BUCARAM**</p>
<p>						    (** Resigned 6 Feb 97)</p>
<p> Tourism..........Napoleon ICAZA</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Administration Secretary........Miguel SALEM**</p>
<p>						    (** Resigned 6 Feb 97)</p>
<p> Central Bank Manager.......Augusto DE LA TORRE</p>
<p> Head of Economic Team...........Roberto ISAIAS</p>
<p> Monetary Board President..........Alvaro NOBOA</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
